{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# OCR & Document Understanding Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: CTC loss + greedy decoder"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import torch"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import torch.nn as nn"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import torch.nn.functional as F"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def ctc_loss(log_probs, targets, input_lengths, target_lengths, blank=0):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    \"\"\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    log_probs:      (T, N, C) log-softmax over vocab including blank at index 0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    targets:        (N, S) int targets (no blanks)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    input_lengths:  (N,) per-sample time steps used"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    target_lengths: (N,) per-sample target length"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    \"\"\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return F.ctc_loss(log_probs, targets, input_lengths, target_lengths,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                      blank=blank, reduction=\"mean\", zero_infinity=True)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def greedy_ctc_decode(log_probs, blank=0):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    \"\"\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    log_probs: (T, N, C) log-softmax"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    returns: list of index sequences (blanks removed, repeats merged)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    \"\"\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    preds = log_probs.argmax(dim=-1).transpose(0, 1).cpu().tolist()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    out = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for seq in preds:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        decoded = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        prev = None"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for idx in seq:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            if idx != prev and idx != blank:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                decoded.append(idx)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            prev = idx"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        out.append(decoded)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return out"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "`F.ctc_loss` uses the efficient CuDNN implementation when available. The greedy decoder is simpler than a beam search and usually within 1% CER of it."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: Tiny CRNN recogniser"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Minimal CNN + BiLSTM for line OCR."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class TinyCRNN(nn.Module):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self, vocab_size=40, hidden=128, feat=32):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        super().__init__()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.cnn = nn.Sequential("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            nn.Conv2d(1, feat, 3, 1, 1), nn.BatchNorm2d(feat), nn.ReLU(inplace=True),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            nn.MaxPool2d(2),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            nn.Conv2d(feat, feat * 2, 3, 1, 1), nn.BatchNorm2d(feat * 2), nn.ReLU(inplace=True),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            nn.MaxPool2d(2),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            nn.Conv2d(feat * 2, feat * 4, 3, 1, 1), nn.BatchNorm2d(feat * 4), nn.ReLU(inplace=True),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            nn.MaxPool2d((2, 1)),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            nn.Conv2d(feat * 4, feat * 4, 3, 1, 1), nn.BatchNorm2d(feat * 4), nn.ReLU(inplace=True),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            nn.MaxPool2d((2, 1)),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        )"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.rnn = nn.LSTM(feat * 4, hidden, bidirectional=True, batch_first=True)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.head = nn.Linear(hidden * 2, vocab_size)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def forward(self, x):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        # x: (N, 1, H, W)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        f = self.cnn(x)                # (N, C, H', W')"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        f = f.mean(dim=2).transpose(1, 2)  # (N, W', C)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        h, _ = self.rnn(f)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return F.log_softmax(self.head(h).transpose(0, 1), dim=-1)  # (W', N, vocab)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Fixed-height input (the CNN max-pools height to 1). Width is the time dimension for CTC."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: Synthetic OCR"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Generate black-on-white digit strings for an end-to-end smoke test."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import numpy as np"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def synthetic_line(text, height=32, char_width=16):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    W = char_width * len(text)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    img = np.ones((height, W), dtype=np.float32)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for i, c in enumerate(text):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        x = i * char_width"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        shade = 0.0 if c.isalnum() else 0.5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        img[6:height - 6, x + 2:x + char_width - 2] = shade"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return img"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def build_batch(strings, vocab):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    H = 32"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    W = 16 * max(len(s) for s in strings)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    imgs = np.ones((len(strings), 1, H, W), dtype=np.float32)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    target_lengths = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    targets = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for i, s in enumerate(strings):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        imgs[i, 0, :, :16 * len(s)] = synthetic_line(s)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        ids = [vocab.index(c) for c in s]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        targets.extend(ids)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        target_lengths.append(len(ids))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return torch.from_numpy(imgs), torch.tensor(targets), torch.tensor(target_lengths)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "vocab = [\"_\"] + list(\"0123456789abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "imgs, targets, lengths = build_batch([\"hello\", \"world\"], vocab)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"images: {imgs.shape}   targets: {targets.shape}   lengths: {lengths.tolist()}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "A real OCR dataset adds fonts, noise, rotation, blur, and colour. The pipeline above is identical."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: Training sketch"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "model = TinyCRNN(vocab_size=len(vocab))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "opt = torch.optim.Adam(model.parameters(), lr=1e-3)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "for step in range(200):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    strings = [\"abc\" + str(step % 10)] * 4 + [\"xyz\" + str((step + 1) % 10)] * 4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    imgs, targets, target_lens = build_batch(strings, vocab)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    log_probs = model(imgs)  # (W', 8, vocab)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    input_lens = torch.full((8,), log_probs.size(0), dtype=torch.long)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    loss = ctc_loss(log_probs, targets, input_lens, target_lens, blank=0)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    opt.zero_grad(); loss.backward(); opt.step()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Loss should drop from ~3 to ~0.2 over 200 steps on this trivial synthetic data."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. **(Easy)** Train the TinyCRNN on 5-digit random numeric strings for 500 steps. Report CER on a held-out set.\n2. **(Medium)** Replace greedy decoding with beam search (beam_width=5). Report CER delta. On which inputs does beam search win?\n3. **(Hard)** Use PaddleOCR on a set of 20 receipts, extract line items, and compute F1 against hand-labelled ground truth for {item_name, price} pairs."
      ]
    }
